        },
        "9": {
            "varname": "lvm_volume_groups_warning",
            "caption": "Lvm Volume Groups: Warning",
            "description": "WARN threshold for how much of a volume group is handed out to logical volumes, in percent. Not set by default, because a volume group with every extent in use is a normal state and not a fault; set it where free space has to be kept for a thin pool or a snapshot to grow into. Supports Nagios ranges. Example: `--warning=90` keeps a tenth of the group free for a pool or a snapshot to grow into.",
